d3d11: isoline tessellation

Applies on top of 0009.

The isoline domain had no workload generator and line output was refused
(UnsupportedTessellationOutputPrimitive).  Each line is now one mesh
workload: dxmt.generate_workload.isoline.* emits ceil(density) lines
(density is always integer partitioned, as in the reference tessellator's
isoline rules) at v = line / lines, each an "inner" edge from (0, v) to
(1, v) with the line detail factor and the workload's padding byte set so
the domain location emits only that edge's points;
dxmt.domain_generate_primitives.line joins them into segments (and the point
generator skips the absent outer edge for isoline point mode).  Line detail
is tessellation factor 0, density 1.  The probe's isolines cases match the
reference tessellator (llvmpipe GL image, the bit-exact D3D12 path); WARP's
own isoline pictures are wrong.

